= Base-rate neglect =

== Overview ==
'''Base-rate neglect''' is underweighting relevant prior or prevalence information relative to case-specific evidence.

== Bayesian benchmark ==
When a task supplies both a base rate and diagnostic evidence, Bayes' theorem specifies how the two should combine under stated assumptions. Responses can depart from that benchmark by giving insufficient weight to the base rate.

== Interpretation ==
Some apparent base-rate neglect depends on how participants interpret sampling, wording, causal structure, or reference classes. The phenomenon should therefore be operationalized against a clearly specified probabilistic model.

